            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for to get back, then the Kannada for to stay overnight."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಪರ್ವತ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪರ್ವತ — parvata — \"a mountain\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆ ಪರ್ವತದ ಮೇಲೆ ಯಾವಾಗಲೂ ಹಿಮ ಇರುತ್ತದೆ. ā parvatada mēle yāvāgalū hima iruttade. There is always snow on that mountain."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬೆಟ್ಟ is a hill; ಪರ್ವತ (parvata) is a high mountain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪರ್ವತ (parvata) is borrowed from Sanskrit parvata, \"a rock, a mountain\" (CDIAL 7945)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
